{"agent_id":"pp3g-cGky-read-only-audit-insurance-review-do-not-modify-files","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T00:30:15.905234484Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"30a3d019-78c2-4801-abbc-809ef26eb9bd","author":"pp3g-cGky-read-only-audit-insurance-review-do-not-modify-files","content":"[PROGRESS] state=midpoint-audit-r2 completed=source-verify+live-verify+test-runs next=result-verdict blocker=none\n\nMidpoint — read-only insurance audit of gh#125 r2 (5ada263a + 7c5b3e88) near complete.\n\nVERIFIED FROM SOURCE (fork 7c5b3e88 @ crosslink/src):\n- v2_file_path_decision: local strict probes (META/CHECKPOINT/V2 branch) -> remote probe -> fail-closed on Err/unreachable/V3; marker-gated fast path; G3 marker write on skip confirmed in live run.\n- Dispatcher covers every v2 caller: sync_v2_readonly, shared_writer hydrate_with_retry, locks_cmd sync_v2_readonly, integrity_cmd (v3->hydrate_from_state, v2->REFUSE->dispatcher), TUI startup sync + background poll.\n- hydrate_to_sqlite module-private (hydration.rs:133); exempts only migrate.rs:266 (explicit v2 import) + integrity_drift.rs:196 (temp DB).\n- 7c5b3e88 daemon fix: dispatcher errors now warn-and-continue instead of aborting the tick loop; semantics restored.\n- G1 v3-join verified in init_cache: remote_v3 check precedes v2 branch; fresh clone joins v3.\n- compact uses hydrate_from_state (safe v3 path); maybe_auto_hydrate has exactly one production caller (main.rs get_db); clear_shared_data callers complete and all gated.\n\nLIVE CONFIRMATION (organic, this session): my trust commits moved the v2 tip -> marker mismatch -> decision Forbidden (remote v3) -> marker refreshed to 655198e0 -> DB intact at 255 issues (grew from 251). The exact old wipe trigger fired in production and the gate held.\n\nTESTS: lib suite 1800 passed 0 failed; all 16 audit-critical tests pass. Integration suite 159 passed 0 failed 4 ignored (finished). Bins suite still running.\n\nFINDINGS (non-blocking):\n1. SHOULD-CONSIDER (LOW): v2_file_path_decision fail-opens when hook-config tracker_remote names a nonexistent remote while other remotes exist (probe skipped -> Allowed). Fix: enumerate remotes; fail closed when ANY remote exists; only zero-remotes may Allowed. Live configs are safe (tracker_remote=origin, valid).\n2. NIT: G6 interim 'missing issues dir' state is not durable — a write path recreates the empty dir (create_dir_all); harmless because read_all_issue_files returns empty for both missing and empty dirs, and hydrate early-returns on empty files.\n3. NIT: no regression test for the 7c5b3e88 warn-and-continue or marker-write-on-skip (latter confirmed live organically).\n\nVerdict trending APPROVE with recorded findings. Next: bins suite completion, then --kind result on #125 (issue stays open).","created_at":"2026-08-08T00:30:15.898007494Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:W8rQwdKJUREaLtmAbdemI6rkSDw+Tvi/qCwUBEnKg1o","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg21041u1Lh4OF9CC79OSsqRwEyf6XClhy7V55d+LtcJQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABARQ5M5LQ/WUeYwr7to+3La2ThVxgmxJ8Pu1xOHkTJ5JXpTl0u8rDmqZLbIM9YFcEpAUzx7+YQNwnq+muIKr8VDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:W8rQwdKJUREaLtmAbdemI6rkSDw+Tvi/qCwUBEnKg1o","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg21041u1Lh4OF9CC79OSsqRwEyf6XClhy7V55d+LtcJQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHn8wXspcLIUkf9R69PxcS8+0IR2u3Dhez9msML0HQnwVAX+FC3mET1MEDvklPdUocyHjnoQX4OktyzcQzo8kQ4="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-cGky-read-only-audit-insurance-review-do-not-modify-files","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T00:36:58.845995123Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"2cc0b407-c661-47da-99a2-25aacb71afff","author":"pp3g-cGky-read-only-audit-insurance-review-do-not-modify-files","content":"Result: AUDIT VERDICT — APPROVE (gh#125 r2, 5ada263a + 7c5b3e88)\n\nIndependent read-only insurance audit of the full finding→fix→verify chain. Every claim in the r2 result was re-verified from source; the acceptance criteria all hold; the hunt found one operator-misconfig-gated fail-open (non-blocking) and three nits. #125 stays open per scope.\n\nVERIFIED FROM SOURCE (fork 7c5b3e88 @ crosslink/src)\n1. Gate (hub_v3.rs:786 v2_file_path_decision): strict local probes (META/CHECKPOINT/V2 branch) where clean-missing (exit 1, no output) is distinguished from detection doubt (→ Err → Forbidden); remote probe via git ls-remote — any non-zero exit → Err → Forbidden; V3 → Forbidden; reachable V2Only/Absent → Allowed; unreachable/unauthenticated → Forbidden. Marker-gated fast path + G3 marker write on skip (live-confirmed).\n2. Dispatcher coverage — no ungated v2 hydration entry point: sync_v2_readonly (locks_cmd:325), shared_writer hydrate_with_retry (206), locks_cmd, integrity_cmd (v3→hydrate_from_state, v2→REFUSE→dispatcher), TUI startup sync + background poll (838/531), daemon v3/v2 split (269–295).\n3. hydrate_to_sqlite module-private (hydration.rs:133); the only two callers outside hydration.rs are deliberate exempts: migrate.rs:266 (explicit v2 import command) and integrity_drift.rs:196 (temp DB). Both safe.\n4. 7c5b3e88 daemon warn-and-continue is a REAL post-commit fix: 5ada263a had `?` on the dispatcher, which would abort the daemon tick loop on any dispatcher Err (lock failures, etc.); the revision restores original warn-and-continue semantics. Confirmed in diff.\n5. G1 v3-join (sync/cache.rs init_cache): remote_v3 check precedes the v2 branch; fresh clones join v3 — correct.\n6. compact uses hydrate_from_state (safe v3 path); maybe_auto_hydrate has exactly one production caller (main.rs get_db); clear_shared_data callers are exactly the two hydration paths (inside transactions) + the gated integrity repair. No other wipers exist.\n7. Discriminating tests present and passing: 8× v2_file_path_decision (incl. remote-probe/forbidden cases), 4× maybe_auto_hydrate, hydrate_v2_safely, G5 inventory, G1 fresh-clone-joins-v3. The new-function tests could not compile against r1 (functions absent) — strongest form of fail-without-fix; the modified-behavior tests assert remote-v3 semantics r1's local-only probe cannot produce.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- No v2 hydration entry point ungated: VERIFIED.\n- Tests fail without each fix: VERIFIED (structurally, see above).\n- Binary sha matches commit: VERIFIED — 0.9.0-beta.1+7c5b3e88.\n- Live tests actually ran: VERIFIED — builder's live hub-tip test passed twice (result comment 00:08) AND reproduced organically this session: my trust commits moved the v2 tip → marker mismatch → decision Forbidden (remote v3) → marker refreshed to 655198e0 → DB intact at 255 issues. The exact old wipe trigger fired in production and the gate held.\n\nTEST EVIDENCE (r2 fork)\n- Lib suite: 1800 passed, 0 failed. Bins suite: 2879 passed, 0 failed. Integration suite: 159 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored. All 16 audit-critical tests pass.\n\nHUNT FINDINGS (non-blocking)\n1. SHOULD-CONSIDER (LOW, operator-misconfig-gated): v2_file_path_decision fail-opens when hook-config tracker_remote names a nonexistent remote while OTHER remotes exist — remote_configured → false → Allowed without consulting the real remote. A repo whose origin hosts v3 would run the v2 path. Fix (≈10 lines): when the named remote is absent, enumerate remotes (list_git_remotes exists); fail closed if ANY remote exists; Allowed only on zero remotes. Live-safe: both ASES hook-configs set valid tracker_remote=origin. Does not block #125 (requires misconfiguration; sync fails loudly in that state); recommended follow-up.\n2. NIT: G6 interim control's 'missing issues dir' state is not durable — a write path recreates the empty dir (create_dir_all at write paths; mtime = rm minute). Harmless: read_all_issue_files returns empty for both missing and empty dirs, and hydrate_to_sqlite early-returns on empty files. Note G6 ran against the r1-era binary; its protection was the empty-files early-return, which held. r2's gate is validated by the builder's live test + organic reproduction above.\n3. NIT: no regression test for the 7c5b3e88 warn-and-continue path, and no unit test asserting marker-write-on-skip (G3) — the latter confirmed live organically instead.\n4. NIT: integrity_cmd repair clears the DB before the dispatcher's locked re-check; a concurrent v3 join in that window leaves an empty-but-recoverable DB (snapshot exists, failure loud). Extremely narrow.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE. r2 closes the gh#125 wipe across every entry point; every uncertainty path fails closed; the production environment is demonstrably safe (organic trigger + intact DB). Residual findings are operator-error-gated or cosmetic; no CONDITIONAL conditions and no REJECT grounds found.\n\nRECOMMENDED FOLLOW-UPS (not blockers): (a) remote-enumeration hardening for the misconfig fail-open; (b) regression tests for warn-and-continue + marker-write-on-skip; (c) consider ordering the integrity repair's clear after the locked re-check.","created_at":"2026-08-08T00:36:58.838634531Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:W8rQwdKJUREaLtmAbdemI6rkSDw+Tvi/qCwUBEnKg1o","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg21041u1Lh4OF9CC79OSsqRwEyf6XClhy7V55d+LtcJQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAet4K1PpktGzoaVKKU32al371bW9WesLPGtIkzBYiA5DG6XBmd2v5Nx8ehIWcO35CralZ0SX8s/tDvORPFiljBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:W8rQwdKJUREaLtmAbdemI6rkSDw+Tvi/qCwUBEnKg1o","signature":"U1NIU